{{!
    @template local_ai_course_assistant/analytics_tab_themes

    Themes tab of the analytics dashboard. Replaces the innerHTML string that
    amd/src/analytics_dashboard.js used to build for this pane
    (CONTRIB-10574 #278).

    Keywords are mined from learner messages, so this is the pane where
    learner-supplied text reaches the page. Mustache escapes it; the old
    string build relied on a hand-rolled escape helper being remembered at
    every call site. The badge value is one of a fixed set chosen in the
    JavaScript, never raw server data, so it is safe in a class attribute.

    The three column headings are still literal English, exactly as they were
    in the JavaScript this replaces.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * chartheight - pixel height for the bar chart canvas
    * rows - one entry per keyword, each with keyword, frequency, category
      and badge

    Example context (json):
    {
        "chartheight": 80,
        "rows": [
            {"keyword": "opportunity cost", "frequency": "34", "category": "concept", "badge": "primary"}
        ]
    }
}}
<div class="row mb-4">
    <div class="col-12">
        <canvas id="sola-chart-themes" height="{{chartheight}}"></canvas>
    </div>
</div>
<table class="table table-sm table-striped">
    <thead>
        <tr>
            <th>Keyword</th>
            <th>Frequency</th>
            <th>Category</th>
        </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
        {{#rows}}
            <tr>
                <td>{{keyword}}</td>
                <td>{{frequency}}</td>
                <td><span class="badge badge-{{badge}} bg-{{badge}}">{{category}}</span></td>
            </tr>
        {{/rows}}
    </tbody>
</table>
